framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0022:
  description |
    Canonical world is unique and viewpoint-free. Two-person cognitive
    relations live in two observer frames. Physical engine effects are
    judged only through canonical state.

problem P1:
  |
    The battle engine lets observer cognition consent with unique world
    facts. targetWorldFailure returns target_unlocalized from
    counterpart.currentAccess before reading placements or mechanical
    distance. executeAction plans hops from the same access. Production
    btl_162854a54de03aa54d93918d1b0feae1 therefore labeled 36 physically
    out-of-area strikes as unlocalized.

premise DRIVER_UNIQUE_WORLD:
  |
    Canonical state is the unique viewpoint-free world: placements,
    topology, body facing, eye direction, organ vision and hearing,
    exposure, and a mechanical distance band between two placements.

premise DRIVER_TWO_COGNITIONS:
  |
    A two-person relation constituted by perception is not unique
    world. It is mutual cognition and may be two frames, A toward B
    and B toward A. Those frames may hide counterpart actions from
    a character. They must not judge physical hits, misses, or hops.

premise DRIVER_PHYSICAL:
  |
    Physical effects (range, hops, damage, organ- or exposure-based
    line of fire) are judged only through canonical state. Mental
    effects may later read cognitive frames; that routing is not
    decided here.

premise DRIVER_SCOPE:
  |
    This record does not delete pairRelations, ActionKind reposition,
    or pair.sight/sound fields. It does not fast-forward hops or add
    a provider call. pair.sight/sound must not be treated as the two
    cognitive frames; relocating occlusion onto areas or objects is
    later work.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Considered options are: leave engine revalidation on the same
    assess path as observer listing; split listing from canonical
    revalidation now and leave pair.sight/sound in place; or delete
    pair.sight/sound in the same slice. Shared assess is the mix-in.
    Field deletion rewrites projection and init. Split now is the
    producing repair.

evidence E_OWNER:
  |
    On 2026-09-06 the product owner stated the unique-world versus
    two-cognition principle, allowed body facing and eye direction
    in unique world, forbade perceptual relations on unique world,
    required physical effects to go through canonical state, and
    left mental effects open. The owner then instructed to record
    that principle as an ADR and to repair the current engine mix-in
    with an llmthink analysis.

evidence E_CODE:
  |
    packages/shared/src/action-feasibility.ts targetWorldFailure
    returns target_unlocalized when perception access is not coarse
    or clear. revalidateCharacterAction spreads that perception into
    assess. packages/shared/src/battle-engine.ts executeAction sets
    hop unlocalized from the same access. docs/battle-action-feasibility.md
    draws revalidation from worldState, then says the engine
    re-evaluates the same rules.

evidence E_BATTLE:
  |
    Production v0.22.0-rc.6 battle
    btl_162854a54de03aa54d93918d1b0feae1 requested counterpart
    strikes, executed reposition, reason target_unlocalized x36,
    perception currentAccess none, placements present in two areas.
    Analysis: docs/canonical-world-and-observer-cognition.llmthink.dsl.
    Hop noop RCA remains
    docs/v0.22.0-rc.6-reposition-noop-id-split-rca.llmthink.dsl.

evidence E_AUDIT:
  |
    llmthink domain KshiaiCanonicalWorldObserverCognition supported
    observer-only listing, canonical-only revalidation, keeping
    mechanical distance and facing in unique world, and deferring
    pair.sight/sound deletion. It rejected treating this slice as
    the area-ID hop repair.

decision D1 based_on P1, DRIVER_UNIQUE_WORLD, DRIVER_TWO_COGNITIONS, E_OWNER:
  |
    Unique world holds placements, topology, body facing, eye
    direction, organ vision and hearing, exposure, and mechanical
    distance. Two-person perceptual relations live only in
    perceptionFrameA and perceptionFrameB.

decision D2 based_on DRIVER_PHYSICAL, E_CODE, E_BATTLE, OPTIONS:
  |
    Observer-safe listing may drop counterpart actions when
    currentAccess is not coarse or clear, and may label targets
    with perceivedAs. Engine revalidation, substitution, and hop
    correction must not read observer frames. Canonical
    target_unlocalized is missing or out-of-scene placement, or
    actor delirious. separate_area and in-area rank misses stay
    out_of_range. ADR-0020 substitution of those reasons to
    reposition remains.

decision D3 based_on DRIVER_SCOPE, OPTIONS, E_AUDIT:
  |
    Do not delete pair.sight/sound in this record. They are not
    the two cognitive frames. Relocate physical occlusion later.
    Do not fast-forward hops. Do not peel ADR-0021 substitution.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-06 the product owner instructed to record this
    principle as an ADR and to repair the current battle-engine
    mix-in, with llmthink analysis.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, E_OWNER:
  |
    ADR-0022 is Accepted at this owner-approved revision.
    Implementation of D1 and D2 in the current engine is
    authorized. ADR-0020 and ADR-0021 remain Accepted.
